<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lithuanian–Byelorussian Soviet Socialist Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Litbel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lithuanian–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byelorussian-ssr">Byelorussian Soviet Socialist Republic</a>, known as Litbel, was a short-lived Bolshevik state formed in February 1919 by merging the Soviet republics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and Byelorussia, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a>. It depended on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> and collapsed when Polish forces took Vilnius in April 1919 and the Polish and Lithuanian armies pushed the Bolsheviks back. It had ceased to exist by the summer of 1919.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lithuanian-byelorussian-soviet-socialist-republic.jpg" alt="Lithuanian–Byelorussian Soviet Socialist Republic" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Lithuanian-Byelorussian_SSR.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
